@nicolas-grekas Regarding default types: I did not want to support providing the default type via a child class attribute because the whole goal of this feature is the extensibility of discriminator maps without having to change them in the parent class but simply by adding the new child class/implementation. The default type is different, in my opinion, because it must be defined in the parent, thus the mapping should also be added there. Otherwise we define a parent that might not actually exist (which would, of course, result in an error message).

But if you disagree on this point, I can also change it so that defaultType can be a type added via child class attribute.

